Package: powerape
Title: Power Analysis for Average Partial Effects
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Jesper", "Wulff", email = "jwulff@econ.au.dk", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Simulation-based power analysis in which the effect size of
    interest is the average partial effect (APE) or the average interaction
    effect (AIE) from a nonlinear model such as probit or logit.
    Researchers specify targets in APE units (probability points); the
    package calibrates the data-generating process, checks feasibility,
    and computes power for detection, minimum-effect, and equivalence
    claims via confidence-interval criteria (Riesthuis, 2024,
    <doi:10.1177/25152459241240722>), including power curves, required
    sample sizes for the smallest effect size of interest (SESOI),
    robustness sweeps over contextual assumptions (Hancock and Feng,
    2025, <doi:10.1037/met0000776>), and citable power statements.
    Supports binary and continuous focal variables, interaction designs,
    parametric (Gaussian-copula) covariates, and covariates resampled
    from pilot data.
